From 76edc8c57d0da31623a389de8f743db9fdc483d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:02:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] nvmf/tcp: grow zero-copy receive vectors on demand

Highly fragmented zero-copy receives can exhaust the inline request or
PDU iovec array and force NVMe/TCP to materialize the payload. Reserving
the maximum number of entries in every object avoids that copy but adds a
large permanent memory cost.

Grow the request, segment-reference, and PDU vectors geometrically only
when the inline capacity is exceeded. Retain expanded vectors for object
reuse and keep the copied fallback at the uint8_t iovcnt limit or when an
allocation fails.

Add unit coverage for growth, reuse, the maximum capacity, and fallback.

Change-Id: I8034ca47c1dced798e7597a8b5955a961fc76d3c
Signed-off-by: Jerome Tollet <jtollet@cisco.com>
---
